1
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:08,860
Two days before the exam. One student, one tablet, and a notebook app he was paying for.

2
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:14,560
Every new notebook was behind a paywall.

3
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:26,120
Bringing in his lecture PDFs? Premium too.

4
00:00:30,950 --> 00:00:35,900
Then, one night, he asked Claude to visualise a damped oscillator.

5
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:39,580
And for the first time, he could see it.

6
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:49,380
But his notes couldn't hold it. A screenshot froze it.

7
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:52,630
The part that made it click was gone.

8
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:58,490
So he asked a different question.

9
00:01:07,450 --> 00:01:10,470
Night after night, they built it together.

10
00:01:10,950 --> 00:01:15,430
Ink that keeps up with a pen. Pages that never go black.

11
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:28,310
Then the first live page ran, right between his notes.

12
00:01:31,950 --> 00:01:34,690
And he could still write on top of it.

13
00:01:44,450 --> 00:01:48,550
Record a lecture, and tap any stroke to hear that moment.

14
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:57,440
Hide a word under tape, and it becomes a flashcard. Sync only if you want, encrypted first.

15
00:02:03,450 --> 00:02:09,330
That student is Archishman. He asked Claude, and together they built OpenNote.

16
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:16,530
Free. No ads. No account. On the web, Android and Windows.

17
00:02:18,950 --> 00:02:23,980
And the code is on GitHub, for the next student who hits the same wall.
